\section{Introduction}
Uzekwe (Zekwe; ISO 639-3 \texttt{eze}) is an Upper Cross River language of Cross River State, Nigeria, per the search results. Joshua Project lists a population of about 19,000 and records Scripture status as ``Translation Started'' and the language as not written. Very little else was found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Zekwe language (Wikipedia): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zekwe_language}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Uzekwe in Nigeria (Joshua Project people-group profile): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15758/NI}
\item Joshua Project language page for \texttt{eze}: \url{https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/languages/eze}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
